# RTL8852BS2 authentication: transmit an Authentication Request to a real
# access point, receive its Authentication Response.
#
# The parent is the active-scan profile whose whole chain already passed on the
# board, so one run of this image re-validates everything proven before -
# firmware download, the runtime control plane, the no-link role and CAM, the
# passive 2.4 GHz 1-13 sweep with real Beacon RX, the wlan0 netdev whose wapi
# scan reports those access points, and the host and firmware transmit paths
# that put a Probe Request in the air and got a Probe Response back - and then
# adds the one new step.
#
# That step is the first frame this port addresses to a single peer. A passive
# sweep picks the access point with the most received Beacons and takes the
# channel it advertises; a second sweep then transmits an open-system
# Authentication Request from inside its receive loop, at the moment the
# firmware reports it entered that channel. Scan offload parks the radio there
# until the host submits the next-channel command, so the dwell is a window in
# which the radio is known to be tuned to the target and the answer can arrive
# on the same channel. The descriptor drops the broadcast/multicast bit the
# Probe Request needs, because a unicast management frame is acknowledged by
# its recipient.
#
# The image fails unless an Authentication frame addressed to the eFuse self
# MAC arrives. A1 is compared in host software, so no register setting can
# make another station's frame count as an answer to this one.
#
# This does NOT associate. The address CAM still holds the no-link role, so
# this host does not acknowledge the response and the access point will retry
# it and time the exchange out. Receiving the response is the result; a link is
# not claimed. Still RAM-only: no key, no data path, no IP address, no wlan0
# behaviour change, and nothing written to eMMC, SPI flash, eFuse or the
# U-Boot environment.

#include "../wireless_scanofld_active_diag/defconfig"

CONFIG_K1_RTL8852BS2_RUNTIME_AUTH_DIAGNOSTIC=y
